  "summary": {
   "status": "complete",
   "text": "Jefferson said he is optimistic about AI's promise to drive productivity and growth while monitoring its effects on the labor market and inflation. He also described potential labor disruption from AI as a real risk. He has framed analysis of AI through the Federal Reserve's dual mandate and financial stability. In October 2026, he said AI adoption is shaping the economy and that AI-related investment has supported business investment and near-term growth expectations.",
